<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34756" root="فو" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفَوًّى</span></b>  <i>Dyed with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُوَّة</span>; applied to a garment;
(T, S, M, K;) and to a hide. (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفَوَّاةٌ</span> A land (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ</span>) <i>abounding with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُوّة</span>: (AHn,
M, K:) or having in it <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُوّة</span>: (M:) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفَبَّاةٌ</span> signifies the same: (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غبى</span>:) or you say
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارض مَفواة من المفاوِى</span> [i. e. ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفْوَاةٌ</span></b> . of which
the pl., without the article, is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفَاوٍ</span>]; (T;) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَفَاوِى</span>
signifying the lands (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَرَضُونَ</span>) <i>that give growth
to</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُوَّة</span>. (TA.)

